// How loud each note of the recording's scales is (dB of full scale, a note's harmonics
// together), key by key from each instrument's lowest: at a middling level, soft, and loud. The
// winds' scales are played at these, so each note can be set beside the recording's at the
// same loudness. Measured from the University of Iowa Musical Instrument Samples
// (docs/citations.md); a note the measuring missed has its neighbours' middle, and each is the
// middle of itself and its two neighbours.

